/-!
# The discrete Stein–Wainger maximal operator

This file was automatically generated by Claude.

This file covers §3 (Reduction to major arcs) and the proof of Theorem 1.1 of B. Krause, J. Roos,
*Discrete analogues of maximally modulated singular integrals of Stein–Wainger type: `ℓ^p` bounds
for `p > 1`*, arXiv:2107.14616v2 ("KR II") (the `ℓ^p` bound for `1 < p < ∞`). It contains blueprint
(`blueprints/discrete-sw.tex`) Lemma 12.2 (`lem:coherence`) and Proposition 12.3 (`prop:finiteSW`)
(the second part of §12) and §13: Lemma 13.1 (`lem:absolute`) and Theorem 13.2 (`thm:main`, eq.
(13.2) `eq:MAIN`), the main result `discrete_stein_wainger_lp`.

Formalization of the blueprint `blueprints/discrete-sw.tex` ("The discrete Stein–Wainger maximal
operator: the combined `ℓ^p` bound, `1 < p < ∞`"). The main result is
`discrete_stein_wainger_lp` (Blueprint Theorem 13.2, `thm:main`, eq. (13.2) `eq:MAIN`): for a
profile `Ω` that is smooth on `ℝⁿ ∖ {0}`, homogeneous of degree zero and of mean zero on the unit
sphere (`IsSWProfile`), the kernel `K(x) = Ω(x)|x|^{-n}` (`swKernel`), the radial polynomial
`P(y) = (y₁² + ⋯ + yₙ²)^d` (`radialPolyZ`) and `1 < p < ∞`, the maximal operator
`𝒞 f(x) = sup_{λ ∈ ℝ} |∑_{y ≠ 0} e(λ P(y)) K(y) f(x - y)|` (`swMax`) is bounded on `ℓ^p(ℤⁿ)`.

## File structure

The formalization is split into the following files, in import order, aligned with the sections
of KR II (and KR I); each former blueprint module is one Lean section:

* `DiscreteSW/Auto/Sec2_1Notation.lean` (KR II §2.1; blueprint §1.2, §14.1, §2):
  sections `Foundations` (the objects of the theorem: `latEmbed`, `radialPolyZ`, `eC`,
  `IsSWProfile`, `swKernel`, `swTerm`, `swOp`, `swMax`) and `Tools` (Lemmas 2.1–2.5);
* `DiscreteSW/Auto/Sec2_2ExponentialSums.lean` (KR II §2.2; blueprint §3): section `Arithmetic`,
  elementary rational approximation and cancellation;
* `DiscreteSW/Auto/Sec2_4_2_5MultiplierApproximations.lean` (KR II §§2.4–2.5, KR I §2; blueprint
  Lemma 2.7, §4, §5): sections `BinaryPartialSums` (Lemma 2.7), `RealVariable` (kernel
  construction and the real-variable multiplier estimates) and `Oscillation` (oscillatory
  integrals and a continuous annular maximal estimate);
* `DiscreteSW/Auto/Sec2_3IonescuWainger.lean` (KR II §2.3, KR I §2.1; blueprint §6, §7): sections
  `Sampling` (sampling and finite Fourier bookkeeping) and `RationalFrequency` (the
  rational-frequency multiplier lemma for pairwise coprime blocks);
* `DiscreteSW/Auto/Sec5MajorArcParameters.lean` (KR II §5, KR I §4; blueprint §8): section
  `MinorArcs`, minor parameter arcs and the choice of the exponent;
* `DiscreteSW/Auto/Sec4MainArgument.lean` (KR II §4, KR I §§6–7; blueprint §§9–11): sections
  `Lifting` (the rational lifting operators and their arithmetic bound), `Truncation` (lifted
  maximal truncations) and `Bands` (lifted oscillatory bands and their assembly);
* `DiscreteSW/Auto/Sec6ErrorEstimate.lean` (KR II §6; blueprint Lemma 12.1): the first part of
  section `MajorArcs`, the kernel-side smoothing error;
* `DiscreteSW/Auto/DiscreteSteinWainger.lean` (this file; KR II §3 and Theorem 1.1; blueprint
  Lemma 12.2, Proposition 12.3, §13): the second part of section `MajorArcs` (coherent grouping
  and the uniform finite dyadic estimate) and section `DiscreteSteinWainger` (the operator on all
